{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793401219,"nonce":"hxsxK6BInmNdcsa+7YGXNQsIDJM=","message":"Text inheritance finding (blocks font-family and the cn typography base): font-size, font-weight, line-height and letter-spacing declared on a CONTAINER do not reach its text children. Only decoration, white-space, text-overflow, text-align and font-style are carried down (InheritedText in stylesheet/base.rs and the tuple loops); TextLook::wanted reads props only from the text node itself. So cn_styles.rs rules like '.cn-button { letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight) }' and the badge font-size rule do nothing for the label text, and font-family has no property at all. Closing this means (1) inheriting those properties through the same three sites, ideally consolidated into one pass, and (2) a tier rule: a Text built with an explicit size/weight must beat an inherited value, otherwise container rules would override every explicit .size() in cn. Needs the Text builder to record which of its font fields were set explicitly. Done so far in this pass: animation:none.","files":null}]}